Module Std.Errors

== Standard exception types are part of the Inox prelude and are documented
== here as the standard-library error surface. They are NOMINAL TYPES, not enum
== values and not classical OO classes.
==
== Exception
==   IOError
==     FileNotFound
==     PermissionDenied
==     AlreadyExists
==     DiskFull
==   ArithmeticError
==     DivisionByZero
==     OverflowError
==     DomainError
==   RangeError
==     IndexError
==
== A typed handler matches the named type and its exception subtypes. Example:
== `On IOError` also handles FileNotFound, PermissionDenied, AlreadyExists and
== DiskFull. The relationship is exception taxonomy only; it does not introduce
== struct/class inheritance, virtual dispatch or general RTTI.
==
== The bootstrap compiler owns these prelude type identities and emits compact
== RuntimeTypeId values. libinoxrt transports those opaque identities without
== knowing the public type names/taxonomy. User-defined exception declaration
== syntax and payload/reflection remain deferred until separately specified.
